WEBVTT

00:24.720 --> 00:26.160
Hey.

00:26.240 --> 00:32.080
Have you ever thought about going to a
new world that's different from this one?

00:32.720 --> 00:38.880
A place that has hella good food, killer
music, extra fluffy beds, you name it!

00:39.880 --> 00:42.320
C'mon, doesn't that sound great?

00:42.440 --> 00:44.920
Spare me! I'll do anything!

00:51.800 --> 00:52.880
Harley.

00:56.000 --> 00:58.360
I'm gonna take you there!

00:58.520 --> 01:00.520
To a new world!

01:06.280 --> 01:08.760
-Have you double checked the equipment?
-Just finished.

01:08.840 --> 01:11.280
<i>-What about the main program?</i>
<i>-Performing the final check now.</i>

01:11.360 --> 01:14.640
Hurry. Power is our main priority,
so just ignore any small leaks.

01:14.720 --> 01:17.440
<i>Roger that. Unit Two, I need</i>
<i>your support on this!</i>

01:17.600 --> 01:19.960
Everything's ready,
ma'am!

01:20.200 --> 01:21.360
Then start it up.

02:01.000 --> 02:05.560
-Was that perfect or what, Puddin'?
-We're just getting started, honey!

02:05.800 --> 02:09.240
Consider this the prelude
to a very, very long show.

02:17.000 --> 02:18.840
-Harley.
-Yay!

02:22.920 --> 02:26.680
A new world! That's music to my ears!

02:28.360 --> 02:30.720
It's exactly what I've been itching for.

02:41.680 --> 02:46.000
The modern world is so ugly!
And worst of all...

02:46.880 --> 02:48.520
it's unfair.

02:54.440 --> 02:55.760
What's the matter?

02:55.840 --> 02:58.800
The power output is lower than we
expected. It won't last.

02:58.880 --> 03:00.200
Then increase the load.

03:00.280 --> 03:02.080
But that would put too
much strain on her!

03:02.160 --> 03:06.160
There is no "her". Just a tool to open
the Gate. Now do it.

03:16.160 --> 03:18.200
You are totally right.

03:18.680 --> 03:21.560
Deep down, that's what everybody's
thinking about!

03:21.640 --> 03:24.560
Even people who're sitting pretty,
eating good every day,

03:24.640 --> 03:27.800
and bossing around their
countless minions!

03:28.440 --> 03:31.680
You mean, they just wanna blow this pop
stand and go someplace else?

03:31.760 --> 03:34.640
That's right! To a new world!

04:00.600 --> 04:03.120
Can you guess why?

04:03.680 --> 04:05.920
It's because their soul,
or their existence,

04:06.000 --> 04:10.200
or whatever you wanna call it,
is screaming on the inside.

04:10.560 --> 04:14.840
It's saying:
"This isn't who I really am!"

04:15.280 --> 04:16.520
People are so stupid!

04:16.600 --> 04:18.960
But nobody ever takes the leap.

04:19.040 --> 04:21.520
And that's why we're going
to change things!

04:21.600 --> 04:25.480
We'll use whatever it takes, whether it's
guns or these scraps of paper!

04:25.600 --> 04:26.760
Hey, Puddin'?

04:32.200 --> 04:34.720
Let's enjoy a drink before we do that.

04:34.880 --> 04:37.240
Changin' the world is
a tough job, ya know?

04:39.720 --> 04:41.840
Hang back for a bit, 'kay?

04:41.920 --> 04:45.600
Booze tastes all the sweeter when I drink
it while waiting for my lover.

04:50.680 --> 04:52.320
Harley.

04:54.400 --> 04:56.160
You're the best woman alive.

04:56.920 --> 04:59.560
Cuz' I'm your woman, Puddin'.

05:00.400 --> 05:02.520
Hey! Everybody havin' a good time?

05:12.120 --> 05:14.440
Jeez. Is this a funeral or what?

05:15.040 --> 05:18.760
-Welcome in.
-Gimme something sweet. Super sweet.

05:19.680 --> 05:22.840
-Where's KJ? Taking the day off?
-Yeah, called in with a cold.

05:25.640 --> 05:28.920
Fun fact. There's nobody
named "KJ" at this bar.

05:32.000 --> 05:33.640
Puddin'! Don't come in here!

05:35.480 --> 05:38.560
-Ma'am! We really need to stop!
-Just keep going.

05:47.680 --> 05:49.040
Don't stop!

06:28.240 --> 06:31.040
Hey, Puddin'? Come in.
Where are you?

06:59.400 --> 07:02.600
I dunno what a samurai could
have against little ol' me.

07:16.400 --> 07:17.680
Uh, gosh... what a pretty sword!

07:25.200 --> 07:27.360
Your mask needs some work, though!

08:10.320 --> 08:12.600
Do you use an flat iron on that ha...

08:35.120 --> 08:37.960
I'm sorry. The Joker slipped
through our fingers.

08:39.440 --> 08:40.560
That's rich!

08:41.160 --> 08:45.360
No, freakin' duh. My Puddin' would never
get caught by chumps like you.

08:46.040 --> 08:47.640
Wait for me, Puddin'.

08:47.760 --> 08:51.320
I'm gonna find my way
back to you for sure.

08:55.840 --> 08:57.480
This is where it all begins.

08:57.880 --> 09:01.320
We've finally opened the
doorway to a new world.

09:10.520 --> 09:13.160
HALF A YEAR LATER

09:14.560 --> 09:20.040
ADVANCED RESEARCH GROUP UNITING
SUPER-HUMAN, CODENAMED: A.R.G.U.S

09:20.120 --> 09:22.920
Please wait a minute!
Are you out of your mind?!

09:23.400 --> 09:24.840
I've already gotten approval.

09:25.360 --> 09:28.120
But these people are supervillains,
the worst of the worst!

09:28.200 --> 09:31.080
And it's going to come down on my
head if anything goes wrong!

09:32.280 --> 09:36.080
-Are you picking a fight with me?
-Not at all, ma'am.

09:36.160 --> 09:39.160
Well, you've already got a major
problem to answer for.

09:39.240 --> 09:41.520
There's a discrepancy
in the number of supplies

09:41.600 --> 09:43.840
coming into the asylum versus
those going out.

09:43.920 --> 09:46.280
It's been like that ever since
you took over here.

09:47.640 --> 09:49.360
So shut up and do what I say.

09:49.480 --> 09:51.600
Otherwise, you'll spend
the rest of your days

09:51.680 --> 09:53.800
from behind bars instead
of in front of them.

09:54.680 --> 09:56.200
Open it.

09:59.160 --> 10:01.760
That you, Wade?
Hang on, this is the best part!

10:09.000 --> 10:10.400
Hey, I said hang on!

10:13.240 --> 10:15.200
What is this, a surprise party?

10:15.280 --> 10:18.080
Get out.
You're going to do a job for me.

10:18.160 --> 10:21.080
Who are you?
You're not my mom, that's for sure.

10:28.280 --> 10:32.240
Wait, Harley. I've been extra
good to you, haven't I?

10:34.360 --> 10:38.880
I gave you the best possible treatment!
So the least I deserve is a thank y...

10:40.920 --> 10:44.800
Sorry, pal. But there's only one
guy who gets free reign over me.

10:44.880 --> 10:46.680
Both romantically and physically.

10:49.600 --> 10:50.920
Take her away.

10:53.880 --> 10:56.840
Lead me to the next cell.
Hurry up.

10:58.520 --> 11:01.960
You're insane! Nobody in their right
mind would ever let these scum out.

11:02.040 --> 11:03.600
Obviously.

11:03.680 --> 11:06.760
It's impossible to change the world
without embracing insanity.

11:26.120 --> 11:27.520
Yo.

11:28.800 --> 11:30.520
Rise and shine, little lady.

11:31.720 --> 11:33.400
Goddammit!

11:33.520 --> 11:37.040
I wanted Tweety's voice to be the first
thing I wake up to in the morning!

11:37.120 --> 11:38.680
Why I gotta see your nasty face?!

11:39.600 --> 11:41.840
Oh, great. A psycho chick.

11:41.920 --> 11:43.840
Hey. Watch your mouth.

11:44.960 --> 11:47.040
That's no way to treat a woman
who you've just met.

11:47.120 --> 11:50.040
Aw shucks! Now that's more like
it! I'm liking you already.

11:50.600 --> 11:53.800
Gentleman? Where the hell's
your bowtie, then?

11:53.880 --> 11:56.520
I can't deny we're wearing the outfit.

11:56.960 --> 11:58.920
But I'm just built different.

11:59.360 --> 12:01.360
Don't you notice anything
special about my face?

12:01.440 --> 12:04.320
I'm seeing two eyes, two ears,
one nose, and one mouth.

12:06.960 --> 12:09.840
Yep. You're a real looker.
Not my type, though.

12:09.920 --> 12:12.360
Do you two just not watch movies or what?

12:13.200 --> 12:15.280
No way! You're a movie star?!

12:15.360 --> 12:19.840
What about TV? I've watched every
season of "Game of Thrones"!

12:19.960 --> 12:21.000
Just forget it.

12:21.080 --> 12:23.360
Isn't this one of those
"shock and awe" scenes?

12:23.440 --> 12:25.000
No, maybe they're going
with foreshadowing.

12:25.080 --> 12:26.760
Like it's more exciting if they
notice who I am later on.

12:26.840 --> 12:30.840
What's the deal with Jason over there?
Have an accident while shaving or what?

12:30.920 --> 12:32.640
I never make mistakes.

12:32.760 --> 12:35.880
I'm wearing this because people seeing my
face could interfere with my mission.

12:36.520 --> 12:39.800
-Mission?
-That's right. It's a noble cause.

12:39.880 --> 12:44.520
Hold the damn phone. Do you know
the reason they hauled us out here?

12:44.600 --> 12:46.200
Yes, we're on a mission for peace.

12:46.800 --> 12:48.840
Because I don't put in work
for anything else.

12:49.680 --> 12:51.320
Peace? Us?

12:51.400 --> 12:55.160
This is just perfect!
Now we've got a crazy mofo, too.

12:55.240 --> 12:59.200
It's about time you woke up, dirtbags.
Glad to see you're all getting along.

12:59.280 --> 13:00.840
Why of course.

13:00.960 --> 13:05.200
If it's going to be a long wait, then
would you mind untying me?

13:05.320 --> 13:10.120
Don't worry.
We arrived some time ago.

13:11.400 --> 13:15.040
You dirtbags have a mission
to carry out. A noble one.

13:15.160 --> 13:17.520
Now listen to the word of our Lord.

13:19.040 --> 13:22.440
<i>The five of you will work together</i>
<i>with my agent there, Adam,</i>

13:22.520 --> 13:24.240
<i>to conduct a mission.</i>

13:26.160 --> 13:28.920
<i>The reward for success</i>
<i>is a reduced sentence.</i>

13:29.200 --> 13:30.920
<i>To put it simply,</i>

13:31.000 --> 13:33.280
<i>your mission is to establish and</i>
<i>protect a series of bridgeheads</i>

13:33.400 --> 13:35.760
<i>that will serve as the framework</i>
<i>for conducting research</i>

13:35.840 --> 13:38.200
<i>and resource acquisition</i>
<i>in a certain region.</i>

13:41.640 --> 13:44.320
Jeez. You really call that "simple"?

13:44.760 --> 13:48.440
It doesn't count unless you use words that
even dumb school kids can understand.

13:48.840 --> 13:51.600
Besides, why the hell should
we work for you?

13:52.480 --> 13:55.880
<i>Because you've all had bombs</i>
<i>implanted in your necks.</i>

13:56.240 --> 14:00.240
<i>And I can trigger them to explode</i>
<i>at anytime that I wish.</i>

14:02.640 --> 14:05.120
<i>Furthermore, they also</i>
<i>work on a countdown.</i>

14:05.560 --> 14:08.240
<i>Unless it receives a radio</i>
<i>signal sent from our end</i>

14:08.320 --> 14:12.120
<i>the bomb is set to explode</i>
<i>every 72 hours.</i>

14:12.720 --> 14:15.640
<i>In other words, any attempts to escape</i>

14:15.720 --> 14:18.960
<i>or ignore the orders that I give</i>
<i>to you will result in death.</i>

14:26.480 --> 14:31.240
So we're just supposed to wag our
tails and be good doggies,

14:32.600 --> 14:34.120
<i>I hear you have a daughter.</i>

14:36.320 --> 14:38.920
-Sit down!
-Amanda Waller! You bitch!

14:39.640 --> 14:40.840
Mark my words.

14:41.400 --> 14:44.680
Lay a single finger on my daughter,
and you're dead friggin' meat!

14:45.520 --> 14:47.080
<i>There are no more objections,</i>
<i>I assume?</i>

14:50.040 --> 14:52.480
<i>Then follow the instructions</i>
<i>Adam gives you.</i>

14:56.280 --> 14:59.200
All of your gear is stored in
the wooden crates in back.

14:59.480 --> 15:01.880
Get changed and prepare for the mission.

15:02.000 --> 15:04.840
Got it? Don't forget about
bombs in your necks.

15:06.160 --> 15:07.240
Are you sure?

15:07.320 --> 15:11.080
What happens if I cling onto you?
Still willing to blow me up then?

15:11.160 --> 15:13.920
-Why you little...
-I'm just kidding.

15:14.000 --> 15:16.280
You aren't even my type.

15:16.360 --> 15:19.280
By the way, she said there
were five of us just now.

15:19.400 --> 15:20.920
Where's the last performer?

15:21.880 --> 15:24.280
What are you talking about?
The fifth one is...

15:26.320 --> 15:27.960
What happened?!

15:28.040 --> 15:29.840
Hey, cut me loose!

15:32.920 --> 15:34.800
Dammit!

15:35.840 --> 15:37.760
Hey! Get us out of these restraints!

15:47.800 --> 15:49.800
What was that explosion?

15:50.000 --> 15:51.920
Let's go take a look. Follow me!

15:55.320 --> 15:56.720
Shit! Just a little more...

15:57.280 --> 15:59.360
Guess we managed to make a crash landing.

16:06.160 --> 16:07.160
What the hell?

16:26.440 --> 16:28.120
Thanks.

16:28.400 --> 16:30.040
Good grief.

16:37.040 --> 16:39.160
We can get out from this side.

16:40.080 --> 16:42.080
He's a metahuman?!

16:42.240 --> 16:46.440
No wonder he was the only one with that
weird restraining device on him.

16:55.920 --> 16:59.800
Hey. Did you have a part in
"The Lord of the Rings"?

17:00.360 --> 17:01.800
What?

17:11.600 --> 17:14.840
Now that's a hardcore film set.
Which studio is doing this one?

17:14.920 --> 17:16.320
Film set? Seriously?

17:16.400 --> 17:18.360
Hey, where are we?

17:18.440 --> 17:20.480
Is this part of the peace
mission or whatever?

17:20.560 --> 17:22.800
That's right. Our noble cause.

17:22.880 --> 17:24.840
Then, like, explain it.

17:26.400 --> 17:29.000
I'm betting you don't know
jack shit, do ya?

17:33.480 --> 17:34.680
Wait a minute!

17:36.560 --> 17:38.880
It's those meatbags from the Kingdom!

17:38.960 --> 17:40.440
Hey! How'd you get here?!

17:40.560 --> 17:44.520
-Huh? Say what?
-My apologies. We're outsiders, you see.

17:44.640 --> 17:46.200
Where is your producer?

17:46.280 --> 17:47.480
Answer me!

17:49.800 --> 17:53.720
Okay, don't even try to tell me
this is a movie set or a dream.

17:53.840 --> 17:56.480
Cuz under the nasty BO
of these pig freaks,

17:56.560 --> 18:00.440
I can smell something real
friggin' familiar. This is all real.

18:02.880 --> 18:06.640
Wonderful. I love when things
are super easy to figure out!

18:07.000 --> 18:10.480
I have no clue where this is
or who you freaks are,

18:11.520 --> 18:14.880
but you're not on my side, right?!

18:22.840 --> 18:24.880
Metahuman in the form of a shark.
Has the IQ of a kindergartener.

18:38.920 --> 18:41.200
The Maiden of Mischief.
Former psychiatrist.

18:50.960 --> 18:55.880
Anybody who gets in my way or disturbs
the peace is dead! Bloodbath-style!

18:56.160 --> 18:58.280
Violent vigilante who is determined to
achieve peace at all costs.

19:00.360 --> 19:02.680
Disgusting beasts!

19:04.400 --> 19:06.040
Begone!

19:15.320 --> 19:18.080
A shape-changer made of living clay.
Unpopular movie actor.

19:25.040 --> 19:28.120
This is getting us nowhere.
Where's their boss?

19:28.720 --> 19:31.480
You mean, like, a King Piggy?
Probably hiding in their pigsty!

19:32.240 --> 19:33.800
It's that one!

19:34.240 --> 19:37.600
Everyone knows that true villains
have hideous faces!

19:38.240 --> 19:41.240
-True villains are hideous, huh?
-What?

19:41.520 --> 19:43.280
Nothing.

19:52.400 --> 19:54.760
Professional assassin. An expert marksman
who never misses his target.

20:00.200 --> 20:03.040
-Run! Run!
-They killed the boss!

20:04.200 --> 20:06.040
What the hell was that all about?

20:06.120 --> 20:08.800
Who knows? But ignoring
all the pig freaks,

20:08.880 --> 20:11.600
I'm guessing that one's on our side?

20:11.880 --> 20:13.680
She did say five people.

20:13.800 --> 20:16.200
Not sure if we can count that
as a "person" though.

20:16.560 --> 20:18.400
Look who's talking.

20:23.080 --> 20:27.520
Hold on! Do you speak our language?

20:35.760 --> 20:40.880
You guys have been fighting those
pig things, too, right?

20:41.800 --> 20:44.320
That guy is on our side. Probably.

20:47.200 --> 20:48.880
Come, my sword!

20:54.240 --> 20:56.160
Was that a trick? Or some kinda magic?

20:56.240 --> 20:58.880
Oh, I get it! So that's what's going on!

20:59.640 --> 21:02.120
It's okay. Don't worry.

21:03.200 --> 21:05.800
Our apologies for frightening you.

21:06.120 --> 21:07.840
We come in peace.

21:07.920 --> 21:11.040
Excellent! The stories in my reality
were boring me to death.

21:11.200 --> 21:16.520
What a fantastic scenario
he's blessed me with!

21:17.360 --> 21:19.720
Wait, what? What's gotten into you?

21:19.800 --> 21:22.320
Don't you get it?
Look around you!

21:22.400 --> 21:23.720
There's dragons and orcs!

21:23.800 --> 21:26.480
An old-fashioned war fought
with swords and arrows!

21:26.680 --> 21:28.800
This is "Alice's Adventures
in Wonderland"!

21:28.880 --> 21:30.160
The Lewis Carroll book?

21:30.240 --> 21:32.440
But I believe the more common
term in pop culture is...

21:33.040 --> 21:34.600
an "Isekai"!

21:34.680 --> 21:36.480
Isekai?

21:36.960 --> 21:39.760
Oh, goddammit. Give me break.

21:39.920 --> 21:42.760
"Noble cause", my ass.
This is friggin' ridiculous!

21:42.840 --> 21:44.400
Ridiculous?

21:44.560 --> 21:46.920
Did you just call my mission ridiculous?!

21:47.440 --> 21:48.880
Have you looked around?

21:49.040 --> 21:51.000
If this isn't ridiculous, then what is?

21:51.160 --> 21:56.320
No matter how sticky the situation gets, I
always see my mission through to the end.

21:57.360 --> 21:59.920
Don't get in my way!

22:00.400 --> 22:02.120
Huh?! Christ, man. Are you blind?

22:02.240 --> 22:04.760
Who the hell do you think just shot
the pig boss's brains out?

22:06.720 --> 22:11.440
You're looking at the chosen warriors who
were summoned from another world!

22:11.520 --> 22:14.680
Isn't that right? Now bring us before
your king! We'll put an end to this war!

22:15.360 --> 22:17.760
"Anybody who disturbs the peace is
dead"? What the hell was that?

22:21.080 --> 22:24.280
You a peace-mongering nutjob or what?

22:24.520 --> 22:26.560
Hey! I already told you once!

22:26.720 --> 22:29.920
Don't say that kinda crap in front of me!

22:30.000 --> 22:31.640
-You guys are still fighting?
-Peace-mongering nutjob!

22:31.720 --> 22:33.880
You are a dead man!

22:42.040 --> 22:44.640
We just got word that
a new group of strangers

22:44.720 --> 22:46.600
has been brought into the Kingdom.

22:46.720 --> 22:48.440
Beings from another world?

22:48.560 --> 22:50.480
Most definitely.

22:50.560 --> 22:52.840
There is nothing they can do.

22:52.920 --> 22:55.720
Isn't that right,
my trailblazing friends?
